---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-31-retired-buyer-crm-claims.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-31',
  title: 'Buyer management claims brought in line with the product',
  tags: ['accuracy', 'buyers', 'pipeline', 'horses'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 31, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
    Removed or reworded claims about the retired Buyer CRM module across the site, and
    pointed them at the surfaces breeders actually use.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Corrected</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li>Lead scoring is no longer claimed anywhere. Prospects are not scored; the Queue view shows replies owed, follow-ups due, applications back, and deposits outstanding.</li>
      <li>The Inquiry, Viewing, Negotiation, Vet Check, Contract, Closed Kanban is replaced by the real Pipeline: Board, Queue, Table, and By Litter views, with stages from Inquiry through Approved.</li>
      <li>Conversion analytics now describes the funnel by lead source and average days in each stage. Pipeline value, deal tracking, and auto-generated stale-lead tasks are removed.</li>
      <li>Communication logging describes notes, calls, video calls, and emails on each prospect.</li>
      <li>Updated on the client management workflow, the dog, cat, goat, sheep, rabbit, and cattle pages, the home page, the for-breeders page, related-workflow cards, the puppy application template page, and two articles.</li>
      <li>The horse page no longer promises an embryo transfer certificate PDF. That download is not reachable in the product today. The card now says you mark a plan as an embryo transfer when you create it and record the genetic dam and the recipient dam.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</article>
